+            </p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
+          Do indoor cats need enrichment?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>
+              Yes. Indoor cats benefit from climbing spaces, scratching posts, window views, puzzle feeders, and daily interactive play. Enrichment reduces boredom and helps cats express natural behaviors safely.
+            </p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="example">
+        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
+          How often should I clean the litter box?
+          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
+        </button>
+        <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" aria-hidden="true">
+          <div class="details-inner">
+            <p>
+              Scoop at least once a day and fully refresh the box on a regular schedule based on the litter type. A good rule is one box per cat, plus one extra, placed in quiet and easy-to-reach areas.
+            </p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+
